h(37, 900, """Everything beneficial must not produce corruption on earth, even if the act appears permissible!""")

h(37, 1900, """Our Lord is worshipped by being occupied with what is beneficial only. Only. Only. Only. Only. Only""")

t(38, 60, """… That is why He is the companion of the abandoned, the companion of the pushed away, the companion of those no one cares for, because His attributes are not deficient like the attributes of His creation. If all humans died and one servant remained on earth, it would suffice him that his Lord is Ever-Living and does not die.""")

h(38, 500, """It is enough pride and honour for the servants that the Lord, our God, the King, has none of the attributes of His creation""")

h(38, 1600, """Purify hearts of rancour, and the love of the Lord will shade you""")

t(38, 2235, """An honour from the Lord for everyone who lives with a sound heart""")

h(39, 250, """Purify hearts of rancour, and the protection of the Lord will cover you""")

h(39, 1100, """Purify hearts, and the gifts of the Lord will amaze you""")

t(39, 1785, """O people: do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another .. do not hate one another""")

h(39, 2250, """Love of revenge puts you outside the divine selection for reform on earth""")

h(40, 700, """Every person who lives on revenge, you will find his mind dull, as a punishment from Allah to him""")

h(40, 1800, """Allah is angry with those who love revenge, so He distances them from Him, and distances them, and distances them, and distances them, and distances them""")

t(40, 2470, """O man: your Lord created you in the best form, in body, spirit, soul and innate nature. The best form is not in the body only; rather the best form is also in everything in you that is not sensed and touched of matter. So do not descend from your creation that is in the best form, sinking with it to the lowest of the low, turning your upright creation upside down and making yourself a monstrosity …""")

t(41, 60, """… after Allah created you in the best form. Do not take revenge .. do not take revenge .. do not take revenge""")

h(41, 500, """Everyone who lives taking revenge on this one and that one lives the life of rats""")

t(41, 1150, """Our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, Exalted in the heavens and on earth, Exalted with great exaltation, said: "The Day when neither wealth nor sons will avail, except whoever comes to Allah with a sound heart".""")

h(41, 1600, """Whoever dies without purifying his heart toward people, let him blame none but himself""")

t(41, 2235, """Our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, Exalted in the heavens and on earth, Exalted with great exaltation, said: "The Day when neither wealth nor sons will avail, except whoever comes to Allah with a sound heart".""")

h(42, 300, """If Paradise were cheap, all people would enter it. Purify hearts, O servants of Allah .. purify hearts .. purify hearts""")

h(42, 1100, """No door to Allah, our Great Lord, has ever opened without the chief of the door's keys being the heart's purity from rancour toward His servants""")

h(42, 2200, """No guidance has ever been complete without complete purity of heart, and no Muslim has wavered between guidance and misguidance except because he did not want to purify his heart of rancour and revenge""")

h(43, 700, """The heart is a hanging lamp: either it radiates light between heaven and earth, or it burns like coal in the lower darknesses!""")

h(43, 1700, """Intentions are either light or fire: whoever purifies his heart, his heart is lit up, and whoever pollutes it with the self's share turns it into an ember!""")

h(44, 300, """If people knew how the tongue brings down its owner, they would flee to the mountains and speak to none but Allah!""")

t(44, 915, """Do not take revenge.. do not take revenge .. do not take revenge""")

h(44, 1300, """The avenger is among the weakest of Allah's creation!""")

t(44, 1920, """Do not take revenge .. do not take revenge .. do not take revenge""")

h(44, 2300, """The avenger is wicked of soul!""")

t(45, 500, """Do not take revenge .. do not take revenge .. do not take revenge""")

h(45, 900, """The avenger is a devil among humans!""")

h(45, 1900, """If every wronged person took revenge, humans would vanish from the earth and all become devils!""")

t(46, 60, """Do not take revenge .. do not take revenge .. do not take revenge""")

h(46, 500, """Whoever walks the path of revenge is doomed""")

h(46, 1500, """Wrong is clear and right is clear, but there is a soul that commands evil and adorns it; so do not take revenge, do not take revenge, do not take revenge!""")

h(46, 2350, """A person stands with his Great Lord in degrees: whenever he does evil he goes down a degree, until he reaches the bottom in distance after having been in the heights!""")

h(47, 1000, """The tongue lowers and raises, and no person has been tried with anything harsher than the affliction of a loose tongue that speaks without wisdom""")

t(47, 1685, """How many a person lights a fire in his kitchen and the cylinder explodes in the opposite direction from where the one who lit it wrongly stood. Dr. Mabrouk Attia, and in concluding my reply to what he said: he fell from a staircase and his knee broke, so he attributed the decree to himself, saying it is from what my hands earned. This means the opposite of what happened to him was possible, as if the Lord's kindness received him with an honour so nothing befell him; and people have such states: they err and are not even scratched, though they were supposed to suffer a great injury. So why was the Lord with these not merely aware of the event? Why did the Great Lord not allow something in them to break, while He allowed Mabrouk Attia's knee to break?

Two separate cases, not alike, and the act is one: committing an error leading to a fracture, or a wound, or even destruction and death. In one case the person dies, and in another no harm befalls him. The one who died, the decree befell him through an error of his own, and the one who did not die, the decree befell him through an error of his own. The one who died fell and died, and the one who did not die fell and got up at once, unharmed!

So, Dr. Mabrouk Attia, do not say that Allah Almighty's role was only that He knew you would break your knee! He only knows?! And where is His will?!""")

h(48, 250, """The one going down a staircase whose knee broke: it would not have broken except by Allah Almighty allowing it to happen""")

h(48, 1100, """Your decree that befalls you through an act you do is either a punishment of destruction, or a punishment that expiates a sin, or a shaping together with expiation of sins""")

t(48, 1790, """Taking a decree that happens through a cause out of the sovereignty of Allah's overpowering will that governs all decrees, from which only the disbelief and faith of humans and jinn are excepted, this taking it out of the sovereignty of Allah Almighty is a mistake. It is not permissible in Shariah, nor correct, to say that the Lord merely knows what the servant will do, because Allah Almighty created for every person a course of decisive decrees not subject to change (except faith and disbelief), both of which are in Allah Almighty's knowledge before He creates the servant; but far be it from Allah Almighty to write them by force upon a person and compel a person to disbelief or faith. For the Great Lord guides whoever wants guidance, and leaves whoever wants and chooses misguidance to himself and his mind. As for what is other than faith, disbelief, righteousness and corruption, even if the element of a person's relative will is present in them, cutting these chosen decrees off and severing them from the personal system of decree assigned to each person is a mistake. The reason is that the speaker, however high his scholarly rank, has not grasped or experienced the depth of understanding Allah Almighty's decrees.

The Abbasids fell because of known errors they committed. So was the Great Lord's role in the fall of the Abbasid state merely His knowing of the thing? When the Abbasid state fell, the ruling Abbasid family was scattered, and its members were spared coming on the Day of Resurrection as rulers who are held to account for people. Is there not in this a shaping of decrees for people? Baghdad was burned, and how many of millions of people had their conditions changed: the rich became destitute, and people entered a new life, millions of people. Was the role of our Great Lord in all that happened merely that He, holy are His names, knew things would happen, and did He not will, before creating people, to have a will connected with the lives of millions of His servants? Each one of them, when he moved from an earlier decree to a later decree, the conditions of his and his family's test changed, and the test moved, for example, from a wealthy family tested with wealth to a poor family that will now be tested with poverty?!

Our Lord, holy are His names and attributes, did not merely know, Dr. Mabrouk Attia .. our Lord knew, willed and decreed .. Your knee that broke when you ran on the stairs, our Lord knew before you were created that it would break, but it""")

t(49, 60, """broke under His will, and our Lord allowed the decree to happen; it is not merely that He knew and has the news with Him! Allah is Exalted far above that.""")

h(49, 500, """What if a person erred in a movement of his body, resulting in the amputation of both his feet, and he became the most learned of the Ummah's scholars because he devoted himself to knowledge: was the Lord's role in this servant's decree only that the Lord knew, or did the Lord also allow this decree to befall him?!""")

t(49, 1250, """In an interview watched perhaps by hundreds of thousands, Ustadh Dr. Mabrouk Attia said about his fall from the stairs of his house that he was in a hurry when he came down, so he fell and his knee broke, and he added: this is a decree resulting from my complete choice, so it is a trial with what I erred in by my own decision. And he gave another mistaken example when he said that a Muslim's waking for the Fajr prayer is certain to happen by his decision, so any Muslim can either get up or turn off the alarm and carry on sleeping.

So what is right in his words is right and what is wrong in them is wrong. Attributing complete will in choice, O professor of grammar and morphology, is a mistake that must be pointed out, because this is the method that has spread among people regrets, remorse over what has passed and anxiety over what is to come. Your running on the stairs and then falling, yes, is actually your mistake, and your hurry, yes, is your mistake; but you could not have changed this decree even if you had come down calmly. As for your saying that the one who sets his alarm has the will to get up for the Fajr prayer, and if he does not get up he has decided by his own will to turn off the alarm and not get up, it is right where you were right and wrong where you were wrong; for there are a thousand other causes that could forcibly prevent him from getting up, apart from his will directed to getting up, or the choice of turning off the alarm and carrying on sleeping.

Decrees are not this shallow nor this simple. When you fell from the stairs of your house, it appeared to you, from a shallow look at the outward of what you saw, that the cause of your fall was entirely your decision, since you attributed the occurrence of the decree to yourself entirely and made Allah Almighty's knowledge a mere knowledge of the decree that negates His will in all that befalls you that is not a matter of creed. Yet the Lord, glory be to Him, does not like disbelief for His servants; whoever disbelieves has disbelieved by his pure, complete will. But the Lord may have willed to expiate your sins through your pain, and to provide with money the doctor who treated you, and with him the hospital orderly and all the staff in it, because you are one of its customers.

The decree we are driven in happens because we did such and such; this is a truth and there is no dispute about this statement. But its happening through what our hands earned, which is true as our Lord said, does not prevent everything other than disbelief from being a divine will in us: we err and it befalls us without our Lord compelling us to it. Yes, this is correct.

Our Lord is not pleased with disbelief for us, so the only exception based on a Qur'anic text is that disbelief and faith are two purely human choices, entirely by the will of the accountable person.

As for what is other than disbelief and faith, they are various kinds of decrees that happen because of our errors; but Dr. Mabrouk Attia speaks of this as if the matter does not happen under an integrated divine decree.

How do you know that the breaking of your knee was not going to befall you through another accident, apart from your error while coming down the stairs?! So do not focus on the stairs; rather focus on your personal system of decree which you were created to receive in full, and which you must complete, apart from faith, disbelief, righteousness and corruption, which are the only exception (the decree in which a person's will is complete).

The one who turns off the alarm, if he were struck during his sleep by a passing illness that put him in a semi-coma, how would he become with certainty always the possessor of will in getting up from his sleep?""")

t(50, 95, """We see central decrees that happen without an error being committed, because they have great value in the system of our shaping. A doctor's medical error is not of what our hands earned, and a plane's crash is not of what our hands earned in the context of the person's own decree. You do not live cut off from the system of decrees around you, so your idea of a person's complete ability to bring about the decree in which he has choice is not an idea of complete correctness and needs correcting by you!

You do not live in the world as a dry, severed tree stump. The world is a great tree, and each of us in it is a branch connected to the tree. Apart from disbelief and faith, all our decrees are connected to the tree-like system of decree. The thinking of Dr. Mabrouk Attia and others like him through the ages is what builds in people's minds the method of weeping over what has passed and early grief over what is possible, a supposed failure, claiming that a person is befallen only by what his own hand earned, far from understanding the depth of human shaping! How many a person erred by his own will, and when he produced a great work he understood the reason for his error, so his error was in fact a blessing whose wisdom he had not understood. And you, Dr. Mabrouk, perhaps the breaking of your knee is a blessing whose wisdom you do not now know?""")

h(50, 900, """Mabrouk Attia: we have choice in what we have a hand in, right and wrong!""")

t(50, 1685, """The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "The Hour will not come until the Romans land at al-A'maq or at Dabiq, and an army of the best of the people of the earth at that time will come out of Madinah against them. When they line up, the Romans will say: Leave us and those who were taken captive from us (sabaw minna) so we can fight them. The Muslims will say: No, by Allah, we will not leave you and our brothers, and they will fight them..." (narrated by Muslim).

With damma on the sin and kasra on the ba (subu minna): ((this is the most correct according to many verifying scholars such as Qadi Iyad and al-Nawawi)); it means that there are groups from the Romans (Europeans or Westerners) who entered Islam voluntarily, knew the secrets of the Romans and their weak points, and contributed greatly to the leadership of the Muslims' state in a way that hurt the Europeans. So the Romans demand that these be handed over to punish them and make an example of them, and the Muslims refuse to betray their brothers in religion, so the Great Malhama breaks out, because the Muslims realise that day that the European demand is nothing but a "pretext".""")

h(50, 2350, """The state of the end times and the influence of the Roman mind on …""")
